# The doors' two tile layers. The map is `Map0012.json`, and what it is
# for is there: a door that opens and leads to the same map,
# `tests/test_same_door.py`, a hatch the hero stands on,
# `tests/test_own_action.py`, and an awning whose opened page lifts it
# above the hero, `tests/test_above_the_hero_by_its_page.py`. The bushes
# across the middle make two rooms, crossed only by the door's teleports.

# 20x15, 300 tiles per layer
# The two tile layers, in reading order: one id per tile, 20 per line.
# These are the ids the binary stores; what turns them into pictures is
# the chipset. Edited by hand, the count has to stay the same.
